+// WithGPUMemSize sets the device memory each GPU gets, in bytes, and the host
+// memory beside it.
+//
+// Both, because Build refuses a configuration where they differ
+// (cpuGPUMemSizeMustEqual): the shared backing store is sized from the sum, and
+// the driver is told one DRAMSize for the device and the page table is walked
+// against the host half. Changing one without the other is not a smaller
+// configuration, it is a rejected one, so a caller asking for a device with less
+// memory than the default is asking for less host memory too.
